).","verses":11,"father":"Kohath","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"elizaphan_1189","name":"Elizaphan","also":"Elzaphan","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"Uzziel","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"mishael_2090","name":"Mishael","also":"","summary":"A Levite; the eldest of the three sons of Uzziel (Ex. 6:22).","verses":2,"father":"Uzziel","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[6,11,14]},{"id":"eleazar_1062","name":"Eleazar","also":"","summary":"The third son of Aaron (Ex. 6:23). His wife, a daughter of Putiel, bore him Phinehas (Ex. 6:25). After the death of Nadab and Abihu (Lev. 10:12; Num. 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Num. 3:32).","verses":61,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[6,12,16]},{"id":"ithamar_649","name":"Ithamar","also":"","summary":"Palm isle, the fourth and youngest son of Aaron (1 Chr. 6:3). He was consecrated to the priesthood along with his brothers (Ex. 6:23); and after the death of Nadab and Abihu, he and Eleazar alone discharged the functions of that office (Lev. 10:6, 12; Num. 3:4).","verses":20,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[6,12,16]}],"places":[],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[175,175,1121,5070,30,30,3947,4289,4289,5414,784,0,0,7760,7760,7004,7126,7126,2114,784,6440,3068,3068,3808,3808,6680,6680],[784,784,3318,3318,6440,6440,6440,3068,3068,3068,398,398,853,4191,4191,4191,6440,6440,6440,6440,3068,3068],[4872,4872,559,413,175,1931,834,834,3068,3068,1696,559,559,559,7138,7138,7138,7138,7138,7138,6942,6942,6942,6942,6942,5921,5921,6440,6440,6440,3605,5971,5971,3513,3513,3513,3513,3513,175,175,1826,1826],[4872,7121,4332,469,469,1121,